3 The Scenario DSL (Domain Specific Language)
*********************************************

In order to provide an expressive and powerful way to describe test
scenarios, a lot of care has gone into creating a good domain-specific
language, which remains flexible but concise.

   Here follows an explanation of every individual field and parameter
possible, including default or optional ones, as well as some
recommendations.  Unless otherwise stated, the YAML representation of
the Scenario DSL will be used.

   ‘pop_test’ represents the top node under which all other nodes live.

